# udev rules for OpenRevo

Three device classes need rules, and each one exists for a different reason.

`ec_sys` is a debugfs file, so it is not covered by udev at all — the module
parameter and the permissions are handled in `modprobe.d/openrevo.conf` and by
the `openrevo-ec` group. `hidraw` and `backlight` are covered here.

Place as `/etc/udev/rules.d/60-openrevo.rules`, then:

```sh
sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=hidraw
sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=backlight
```

Reloading is not enough on its own: the rules only apply to devices that are
retriggered, and `uaccess` needs an active session, so log out and back in after
installing.

```udev
# --- ITE 8291 class keyboard RGB controllers ---------------------------------
# 048d:600b is what the per-key boards report; 048d:ce00 is the same controller
# behind a different PID on newer chassis. Both speak the 0x33 report protocol
# that driver/hid_ffi.rs drives. TAG uaccess hands the node to the logged-in
# seat instead of requiring the input group for the raw HID path.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="048d", ATTRS{idProduct}=="600b", TAG+="uaccess", MODE="0660"
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="048d", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ce00", TAG+="uaccess", MODE="0660"

# --- Backlight ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Writing /sys/class/backlight/*/brightness needs either the video group or
# uaccess. The daemon runs as the user, so uaccess is the right tag.
SUBSYSTEM=="backlight", TAG+="uaccess"

# --- ACPI EC via ec_sys ------------------------------------------------------
# ec_sys is debugfs, not udev, but the write_support parameter is required or the
# module mounts read-only and every bank-0 write silently fails.
# This is the matching modprobe.d file; keep them installed together.
```

The matching `modprobe.d` file (`/etc/modprobe.d/openrevo.conf`):

```modprobe.conf
options ec_sys write_support=1
```

`/etc/modules-load.d/openrevo.conf`:

```text
ec_sys
```

Note the privilege split that results:

| channel | who needs what |
| :--- | :--- |
| `/dev/input/event*` | members of `input` (passive read, no grab) |
| `/sys/kernel/debug/ec/ec_sys` | root (debugfs is 0700 even with the write parameter) |
| ACPI EC ports `0x62`/`0x66` | root or `CAP_SYS_RAWIO` (`ioperm`) |
| `/dev/hidraw*` | logged-in seat via `uaccess` |
| `/sys/class/backlight/*` | logged-in seat via `uaccess` |
| `/dev/rfkill` | root or `CAP_NET_ADMIN` |
